{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>So Lot chose for himself all the plain of the Jordan.</b> He chose that entire region so that he alone, with his shepherds, could seek pasture there — and so that Abraham and his shepherds would not be able to be there." "<b>And Lot journeyed from the east.</b> He did not travel to the right or to the left — that is, north or south — but traveled from east to west, in order to distance himself from Abraham, whose dwelling was in the eastern part of the land of Israel near Ai, where the tribes first came up into the land when they arrived from across the Jordan eastward (Joshua 4)." "<b>And they parted, each man from his brother.</b> Not in pasture alone, but also in their dwelling."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:00.369027584Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}